  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ENV: Sustainable management of  Tsavo and Amboseli  landscapes for resilient communities and ecosystems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kenya):  .Through this activity, FY 2022 funds will scale-up landscape-level biodiversity conservation in areas that fall outside government protected areas in the Tsavo and Amboseli Ecosystems. Specifically, the activity will strengthen Kenyan institutions&apos; capacity to foster a coordinated approach that enhances local stewardship, benefit sharing and the sustainable management of wildlife and biodiversity within the Tsavo and Amboseli Ecosystems. The activity will support improved governance of the landscapes, reduce threats and improve biodiversity conservation, increase partnerships for economic growth, and improve community and ecosystem resilience. In terms of climate adaptation, the activity will increase the community&apos;s ability to withstand environmental shocks and stressors through livelihood development and private sector engagement efforts; as well as conservancy / landscape management plans that set forth adaptation and preparedness measures in the region. .The activity will also focus on strengthening policies in natural capital; catalyzing private sector investments, and providing economic opportunities for women and youth. It will also promote research, monitoring, and learning through data analytics and knowledge management. The activity will also prioritize enhanced collaboration and partnerships with the private sector, conservancies, government, civil society, and other development partners working in the two landscapes.  Ultimately, the activity will strengthen local institutions, expand wildlife space, improve livelihoods for communities, and establish partnerships with the private sector. The activity aligns with the U.S. government priorities through building local organizational capacities to drive local development. The activity also supports USAID&apos;s Biodiversity Policy, the U.S. National Strategy for Combating Wildlife Trafficking, Eliminate, Neutralize and Disrupt (END) Wildlife Trafficking Act and climate change. ....</narrative>
  </description>
